   "claims": [
    "Bench Press Calculator - Find Your 1RM Hello athlete!",
    "🥇 Add your last bench press record 💪 Weight lifted Number of repetitions Below, you see your one-rep max, the maximum weight you could lift at 1 repetition 😎, your 100% effort.",
    "Check out 4 similar weightlifting calculators 🏋️ One-rep max Wilks 531 lifting Build your calculator with Builder Add as preferred on Google With the bench press calculator, you can find your one-rep max.",
    "Using a bench press calculator is necessary to determine this number because it's difficult to accurately guess the exact weight, taking into account the fatigue you may experience from trying multiple 1RM.",
    "Then, knowing the 1 rep max, try the 90% value.",
    "For example, if I lift 80 kg and manage to do 8 reps today, my 90% of one rep max is 91 kg, according to our bench press calculator.",
    "The max bench calculator formula The formula for the max bench calculator uses the following variables: 1 R M 1RM – One-rep max; 𝑤 w – Weight; and 𝑟 r – Number of repetitions (reps).",
    "It is a \"submaximal\" method of finding your one-rep max, as it may underestimate or overestimate your 1RM because it is only a prediction.",
    "When the bench is set at an incline (15-30 degrees), it allows for more shoulder activation than the flat bench press itself.",
    "Form and technique of proper incline bench pressing: Set a bench incline at 15-30 degrees."
   ],
